  (wire (pts (xy 124.46 95.25) (xy 124.46 97.79)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid 37036388-27cb-5767-be19-05f8dea6191b))
  (text "NOTES\n1. U1 Raspberry Pi Pico 2 W is removable: it plugs into two 1x20 2.54 mm female sockets.\n2. U2 GY-521 already has a 3.3 V LDO and I2C pull-ups on the module. No extra pull-ups here.\n3. Sensor VCC is fed from 3V3(OUT) (pin 36) only. Never from VBUS or VSYS.\n4. AD0 is tied to GND (I2C address 0x68) by one short BOTTOM-layer trace. Cut it to free AD0.\n5. INT -> GP2 (pin 4), optional data-ready interrupt. XDA/XCL unused.\n6. Firmware: Wire.setSDA(4); Wire.setSCL(5); Wire.begin();  GP4 = SDA = pin 6, GP5 = SCL = pin 7.\n7. J1 = optional I2C/test header (3V3, GND, SCL, SDA, INT) for a logic analyser or a 2nd sensor." (at 25.4 162.56 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 1f4dfbbb-1fd6-52c7-b750-96cd48fa61f9))
  (text "PCB: 57 x 52 mm, 2 layers, antenna cut-out 14 x 9 mm under the Pico antenna (per RPi datasheet)." (at 25.4 190.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid b7a22517-94ab-5b7d-b4d8-c8b9247f5d85))
